# What it does NOT yet do

This is the gap I'd fix before calling it the finished analytics system.

The snapshot script currently snapshots **account/integration analytics only**.

It does **not yet automatically**:

```text
discover every published post
        ↓
retrieve analytics for each post
        ↓
snapshot each repeatedly
        ↓
join them to OUR content ID
        ↓
calculate comparable derived metrics
        ↓
display everything in our own dashboard
```

The pieces are available. The orchestration isn't built.

Postiz's API can list posts over a date range and returns the integration and release URL for each one, so we can programmatically discover published content. ([Postiz Documentation][5])

The proper collector becomes:

```text
every hour
   │
   ├── enumerate 15 integrations
   │
   ├── snapshot account metrics
   │
   ├── enumerate published posts
   │
   ├── fetch each post's metrics
   │
   ├── append observations
   │
   └── update derived statistics
```

