# And snapshot analytics at fixed ages

This is more important than simply requesting "last 30 days."

For every publication:

```text
T+15m
T+1h
T+3h
T+6h
T+12h
T+24h
T+48h
T+7d
T+30d
```

store a snapshot.

Now we can derive:

```text
velocity_1h
velocity_6h
velocity_24h

growth_1h_to_6h
growth_6h_to_24h

likes_per_1k_views
comments_per_1k_views
shares_per_1k_views
followers_per_1k_views
```

And compare things fairly:

```text
TikTok raptor at +6 hours
```

against:

```text
TikTok T-Rex at +6 hours
```

rather than comparing one seven-day-old video against one 20-minute-old video.

That distinction is huge.

